", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Aaron Bean (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Aaron Bean seeks reelection in this northeastern Florida district, which leans Republican by about five points at the presidential level. He enters the fall with a decisive financial advantage, having raised roughly $2.2 million and holding $1.6 million on hand, while Democratic nominee LaShonda Holloway has raised about $27,000. Minor third-party and independent candidates trail far behind in resources.\n\nRaters across the spectrum place the seat in the Republican column: half call it Solid or Safe Republican, and the rest call it Likely Republican. Prediction markets price Bean's chances near 85 percent. Holloway emerged from a contested primary and has drawn some high-profile endorsements, but with minimal fundraising and no public polling in the race, she faces a steep structural disadvantage. The forecast expects Bean to win by a double-digit margin, with residual uncertainty reflecting the absence of district-level polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0948, "margin": -8.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0811, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0937, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0773, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0859, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0659, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0699, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0664, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1209, "margin": -8.3}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0854, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0503, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0799, "margin": -9.0},